{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-d055063e-8641-45db-9249-095d3d08e286","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b6b4f7a1159f465","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-dvw25u6y/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E003.md","content":"# External OIDC authentication integration for MaaS on xKS\n\n## Description\n\nReplaces OpenShift's built-in OAuth/TokenReview-based user identity with external OIDC validation for MaaS on xKS. Managed Kubernetes services (CKS, AKS, EKS, GKE) do not expose OpenShift's identity infrastructure, so customers bring their own OIDC-compatible identity provider (Keycloak, Entra ID, Google Identity Platform, Cognito, or other standards-compliant providers) and Authorino validates JWT bearer tokens against it. API key authentication (the `sk-oai-*` flow) remains unchanged and OIDC-independent.\n\nThis work assumes Kuadrant/Authorino-based authentication enforcement. It is gated on the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation: if the direct Envoy ext_authz contingency is selected (neither official RHCL charts nor standalone Kuadrant viable), the enforcement integration is reworked to the Envoy-native approach.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Configure the MaaS AuthPolicy / Authorino authentication to use the external OIDC identity source (issuer URL, JWKS endpoint, audience) in place of KubernetesTokenReview against the OpenShift API server.\n- Adapt OpenShift-specific identity assumptions in maas-api (internal token-validation paths that rely on Kubernetes TokenReview, SubjectAccessReview, and OpenShift identity mapping) for the xKS identity model.\n- Preserve the API key validation flow via the maas-api callback path (`/internal/v1/api-keys/validate`) — it must remain OIDC-agnostic.\n- Resolve and implement the OIDC validation behavior during identity-provider outages (caching/failure strategy — open question owned by Security / MaaS Engineering; an implementation decision, not a scope unknown).\n- Document the configuration requirements for standards-compliant OIDC providers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a MaaS deployment with an external OIDC provider configured, when a user authenticates with a valid OIDC JWT token and creates an API key, then the API key is persisted in PostgreSQL and can be used for model inference, measured by a successful inference request using the generated API key.\n- Given the OIDC provider becomes unavailable (network partition or IdP downtime), inference requests using valid API keys continue to succeed (API key validation is OIDC-independent), while OIDC-authenticated requests fail with HTTP 503 and a descriptive error message, measured by response status and error body.\n- Given an invalid or expired OIDC JWT, the request is rejected with an appropriate error.\n- The OIDC validation behavior during IdP outages (caching strategy) is documented and implemented.\n- The change is additive/configuration-driven: RHOAI MaaS GA identity behavior is unchanged when OpenShift identity is used (backwards-compatibility NFR).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-4 (P0): External OIDC authentication validated for user identity.\n- HLR-5 (P0): API key authentication (`sk-oai-*` flow) functional on xKS (preserved and regression-verified by this epic).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Architecture context (models-as-a-service.md) confirms the AuthPolicy already supports API key extraction, Kubernetes TokenReview, and optional OIDC JWT validation — the work is reconfiguring and hardening the OIDC path as the primary identity source on xKS.\n- The strategy's open question \"Can we leverage existing MaaS AuthPolicy with external OIDC, or are changes needed?\" is resolved by this epic's implementation; both outcomes are within its scope.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":83338,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3d12adea12401d9","agent_id":"a585326c42577ebb9","session_id":"03f22d79-03f4-4cd2-8583-e4fd3448986e","uuid":"f9abbaa2-0337-4542-8459-7588dd0c4e71","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:58:39.689Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
