{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b3676e02-3fea-4d02-9fae-1805c91b0dc9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-81adca0ec69df743","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-dvw25u6y/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E005.md","content":"# Prometheus metrics instrumentation in maas-api\n\n## Description\n\nAdds Prometheus metrics instrumentation to maas-api covering token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle, and inference latency. Observability is a core value proposition of MaaS on xKS per the strategy, and metrics are its P0 tier. This is Tier 1 work — the instrumentation is independent of the RHCL/Kuadrant support outcome and of the deployment platform.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Prometheus metrics in maas-api for:\n  - API key lifecycle events (creation, validation, revocation).\n  - Token usage per user/subscription.\n  - Rate limiting enforcement (including exceeded-quota events).\n  - Inference request latency.\n- Exposure via the Prometheus-compatible `/metrics` endpoint on the existing dedicated metrics listener.\n- Asynchronous metric emission to bound latency overhead, with the strategy's mitigation applied if needed (if p99 overhead exceeds 5 ms, move emission to post-response goroutines).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a deployed MaaS instance with Prometheus integration, when a user creates an API key, makes inference requests, and exceeds a rate limit, then Prometheus metrics include `maas_api_key_created_total`, `maas_inference_requests_total{user, model, subscription}`, and `maas_rate_limit_enforced_total{user, model, exceeded_quota}`, measured by querying the Prometheus instance.\n- Metric emission overhead on the request path stays within the strategy's p99 5 ms bound, or emission is moved to post-response processing.\n- The instrumentation is additive: RHOAI MaaS GA behavior is unchanged (backwards-compatibility NFR).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-8 (P0): Observability metrics functional — token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle events (instrumentation half; dashboard and CKS Prometheus integration are covered by the observability integration epic).\n\n## Notes\n\n- The strategy's assumption \"observability instrumentation in maas-api does not require MaaS 3.4 GA code changes — needs validation\" is resolved during implementation: if the 3.4-based build cannot take the change in place, it lands as a post-3.4 patch (an implementation decision within this epic's scope).\n- Architecture context confirms maas-api already has a Prometheus client dependency and a dedicated metrics listener (port 9090), so this extends an existing foundation rather than introducing new infrastructure.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":85050,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3d12adea12401d9","agent_id":"a585326c42577ebb9","session_id":"03f22d79-03f4-4cd2-8583-e4fd3448986e","uuid":"1aaa5c3e-4080-4cac-a79d-5913340a0003","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:58:59.784Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
