eded quota) and subscription selection decisions appear as structured entries retrievable from CKS Grafana Loki.\n- Logging does not block the request path (asynchronous or bounded-latency emission).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-10 (P1): Observability logging functional — authentication events, rate limit enforcement, subscription selection (MaaS-side instrumentation and Loki integration; Kuadrant-side logging configuration is part of the selected deployment mechanism).\n\n## Notes\n\n- CKS Grafana Loki is assumed available per the strategy (CoreWeave standard infrastructure); accessibility is validated with the CKS infrastructure validation pass.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":88008,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3d12adea12401d9","agent_id":"a585326c42577ebb9","session_id":"03f22d79-03f4-4cd2-8583-e4fd3448986e","uuid":"1511bd76-f52c-4e33-a89d-1410e2591be2","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:59:40.049Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
