{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-8766ea96-12c8-4f95-856a-4813fe833677","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-94e793f005eb6c98","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-dvw25u6y/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-A-E012.md","content":"# Deploy Kuadrant on xKS via official RHCL Helm charts (Branch A)\n\n## Description\n\nBranch A of the RHCL/Kuadrant deployment mechanism: RHCL officially supports xKS and provides Helm charts. Deploys Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) on CKS — the priority platform — via the official RHCL Helm charts, with Authorino configured for external OIDC validation (replacing KubernetesTokenReview) and structured logging for authentication decisions and rate-limit enforcement. The mechanism is reusable for the AKS deployment. This branch epic applies only if the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation selects outcome A (official RHCL Helm charts committed and viable).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Install the official RHCL/Kuadrant Helm charts on a CKS cluster with the Istio GatewayClass.\n- Configure Authorino for external OIDC identity validation (issuer URL, JWKS endpoint, audience) and provide OIDC configuration guidance for the MaaS AuthPolicy integration.\n- Structured logging for authentication decisions (Authorino) and rate limit enforcement (Limitador), formatted for CKS Grafana Loki aggregation.\n- Validate that TokenRateLimitPolicy enforcement works on the CKS deployment (rate limiting is K8s-platform-agnostic per the strategy).\n- Confirm the mechanism carries over to AKS.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) is installed via the official RHCL Helm charts on a CKS cluster, with all pods healthy.\n- Authorino validates external OIDC JWTs against a configured issuer (valid tokens accepted, invalid/expired tokens rejected).\n- Structured authentication-decision and rate-limit-enforcement log entries are produced and retrievable from CKS Grafana Loki.\n- A MaaSSubscription with token rate limits configured returns HTTP 429 when the quota is exceeded (TokenRateLimitPolicy enforcement functional on CKS).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 (P0): RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (this branch realizes the mechanism).\n- HLR-3 (P0): Token rate limiting functional on xKS (Limitador enforcement path).\n- HLR-10 (P1): Observability logging functional (Authorino/Limitador structured logging half).\n\n## Notes\n\n- This is a conditional branch epic (branch A), gated by the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation; it is attached to that investigation as a plan document and is not a standalone Jira issue.\n- Gate failure impact: if outcome A does not hold (RHCL does not commit official xKS support), this epic is removed and the standalone Authorino + Limitador Helm deployment (branch B) applies instead.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":89853,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3d12adea12401d9","agent_id":"a585326c42577ebb9","session_id":"03f22d79-03f4-4cd2-8583-e4fd3448986e","uuid":"c8fa6b0d-ec19-4bab-83d8-0b242d5c01c9","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:00:08.664Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
