{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-2a21930e-69d2-4ebb-ac06-88f550b19702","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-96733d41d7abed95","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-dvw25u6y/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-C-E012.md","content":"# Direct Envoy ext_authz integration for MaaS auth and rate limiting (Branch C)\n\n## Description\n\nBranch C of the RHCL/Kuadrant deployment mechanism (contingency): neither the official RHCL Helm charts nor standalone Kuadrant deployment is viable, so MaaS authentication and rate-limiting enforcement are integrated directly with Envoy ext_authz at the gateway, bypassing Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador). This reworks the MaaS-side enforcement integration while preserving the external OIDC validation and API key flows. This branch epic applies only if the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation selects outcome C.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Design and implement Envoy-native authentication enforcement via ext_authz covering the OIDC JWT validation path and the API key validation path (the maas-api callback validation flow).\n- Define the rate-limiting enforcement approach without Limitador's TokenRateLimitPolicy, preserving per-subscription token rate limits with HTTP 429 on exceeded quota (or a documented equivalent).\n- Preserve the strategy's identity model: customer-provided OIDC provider, API keys OIDC-independent.\n- Keep changes additive/configuration-driven so RHOAI MaaS GA behavior is unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A design for Envoy-native enforcement exists covering OIDC JWT validation and API key validation at the gateway, reviewed and recorded.\n- Enforcement is integrated with the gateway on a CKS cluster with equivalent behavior to the Kuadrant path: valid OIDC tokens and API keys accepted; invalid credentials rejected; exceeded token quotas return HTTP 429 (or the documented equivalent with rationale).\n- RHOAI MaaS GA behavior is unchanged (additive/configuration-driven change only).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 (P0): RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (this branch realizes the contingency mechanism).\n- HLR-3 (P0): Token rate limiting functional on xKS (Envoy-native enforcement path).\n- HLR-4 (P0) / HLR-5 (P0): external OIDC and API key authentication remain functional under the reworked enforcement (the primary OIDC integration epic is rewritten accordingly on this branch).\n\n## Notes\n\n- This is a conditional branch epic (branch C), gated by the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation; it is attached to that investigation as a plan document and is not a standalone Jira issue.\n- Gate failure impact: if the contingency also fails, the work is rewritten — escalate to product leadership and reassess the MaaS xKS Dev Preview scope, per the strategy's risk mitigation (\"lack of official RHCL support undermines the long-term viability of MaaS on xKS\").\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":91377,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3d12adea12401d9","agent_id":"a585326c42577ebb9","session_id":"03f22d79-03f4-4cd2-8583-e4fd3448986e","uuid":"d0685024-74d8-4d25-8a68-ab5fa8a06528","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:00:29.292Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
