{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f806dfc85aa53ce","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n3\ttitle: MaaS Helm chart packaging for xKS deployment\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# MaaS Helm chart packaging for xKS deployment\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tPackages the MaaS components (maas-api, maas-controller, and the payload-processing Envoy external processor) as Helm charts installable on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (xKS: CKS, AKS, EKS, GKE), replacing the OLM-based operator installation used on RHOAI. The charts expose configuration for everything that is OpenShift-specific today: gateway class, identity provider, TLS certificate source, and database connection. This is Tier 1 work — it delivers value regardless of how the RHCL/Kuadrant support question resolves.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Helm charts for maas-api, maas-controller, and the payload-processing ext_proc component, with configurable values for:\n38\t  - GatewayClass name (Istio for CKS; other implementations for other xKS platforms) instead of `openshift-default`.\n39\t  - External OIDC issuer configuration (issuer URL, client ID, audience, group claim path).\n40\t  - TLS certificate source via cert-manager, replacing OpenShift service-CA auto-generated certificates.\n41\t  - PostgreSQL connection, supporting either a dedicated database or one shared with other RHAII components.\n42\t- Removal of OpenShift-specific packaging assumptions from the xKS installation path: no OLM dependency; CRDs and validating admission webhooks installed via the chart on non-OLM clusters.\n43\t- Helm chart build pipeline in the repository's existing Konflux-based build infrastructure.\n44\t- Composability with the wider RHAII xKS installation tooling (installable standalone and as part of the RHAII xKS deployment).\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- `helm install` of the chart on a non-OpenShift Kubernetes cluster results in running and healthy maas-api and maas-controller pods, measured by pod readiness checks passing.\n49\t- The MaaS HTTPRoutes attach to a configurable GatewayClass (not `openshift-default`), verified with an Istio GatewayClass on a CKS-compatible environment.\n50\t- Chart values allow configuring the OIDC issuer (URL, client ID, audience), the group claim path, the TLS certificate source via cert-manager, and the PostgreSQL connection (shared or dedicated) without modifying the chart.\n51\t- TLS certificates issued via cert-manager renew before expiration without manual intervention.\n52\t- The Helm chart build pipeline produces publishable chart artifacts (build pipeline green).\n53\t- The xKS installation path contains no OLM dependency (Helm-only installation per the strategy's out-of-scope statement on operator integration).\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- Enables HLR-1 (P0): MaaS successfully deployed on CKS.\n58\t- Enables HLR-2 (P0): MaaS successfully deployed on AKS.\n59\t- Supports HLR-4 (P0): provides the configuration surface for external OIDC issuer settings.\n60\t\n61\t## Notes\n62\t\n63\t- The Helm chart build pipeline prerequisite is listed in the strategy as \"Pending human review\"; it is folded into this epic as an acceptance criterion rather than a separate onboarding epic, because the repository is already Konflux-onboarded for container images (per architecture context).\n64\t- The shared-vs-dedicated PostgreSQL decision (open question owned by xKS Platform) is a deployment choice; the chart supports both, so it does not gate this epic.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a608d0b6c1ea84d3","agent_id":"a8dbaf530c1362791","session_id":"03f22d79-03f4-4cd2-8583-e4fd3448986e","uuid":"9b4d32a5-7a0c-4158-b416-1cacb6038866","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:04:25.147Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f806dfc85aa53ce","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
