{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aadc78bc434aa854","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E005\n3\ttitle: Prometheus metrics instrumentation in maas-api\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: -1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Prometheus metrics instrumentation in maas-api\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tAdds Prometheus metrics instrumentation to maas-api covering token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle, and inference latency. Observability is a core value proposition of MaaS on xKS per the strategy, and metrics are its P0 tier. This is Tier 1 work — the instrumentation is independent of the RHCL/Kuadrant support outcome and of the deployment platform.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Prometheus metrics in maas-api for:\n38\t  - API key lifecycle events (creation, validation, revocation).\n39\t  - Token usage per user/subscription.\n40\t  - Rate limiting enforcement (including exceeded-quota events).\n41\t  - Inference request latency.\n42\t- Exposure via the Prometheus-compatible `/metrics` endpoint on the existing dedicated metrics listener.\n43\t- Asynchronous metric emission to bound latency overhead, with the strategy's mitigation applied if needed (if p99 overhead exceeds 5 ms, move emission to post-response goroutines).\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance with Prometheus integration, when a user creates an API key, makes inference requests, and exceeds a rate limit, then Prometheus metrics include `maas_api_key_created_total`, `maas_inference_requests_total{user, model, subscription}`, and `maas_rate_limit_enforced_total{user, model, exceeded_quota}`, measured by querying the Prometheus instance.\n48\t- Metric emission overhead on the request path stays within the strategy's p99 5 ms bound, or emission is moved to post-response processing.\n49\t- The instrumentation is additive: RHOAI MaaS GA behavior is unchanged (backwards-compatibility NFR).\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- HLR-8 (P0): Observability metrics functional — token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle events (instrumentation half; dashboard and CKS Prometheus integration are covered by the observability integration epic).\n54\t\n55\t## Notes\n56\t\n57\t- The strategy's assumption \"observability instrumentation in maas-api does not require MaaS 3.4 GA code changes — needs validation\" is resolved during implementation: if the 3.4-based build cannot take the change in place, it lands as a post-3.4 patch (an implementation decision within this epic's scope).\n58\t- Architecture context confirms maas-api already has a Prometheus client dependency and a dedicated metrics listener (port 9090), so this extends an existing foundation rather than introducing new infrastructure.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a608d0b6c1ea84d3","agent_id":"a8dbaf530c1362791","session_id":"03f22d79-03f4-4cd2-8583-e4fd3448986e","uuid":"321d3777-edaa-4828-8de0-e3db239a95e6","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:04:32.206Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aadc78bc434aa854","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
