{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a04e998b15d8e4e4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E006\n3\ttitle: Perses dashboards and CKS Prometheus integration for MaaS observability\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Monitoring\n6\tteam: xKS Platform\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E005\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E007\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 0\n17\t  open_questions: -1\n18\t  external_dependency: -1\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 0\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: Medium\n25\tai_implementability_score: 0\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Perses dashboards and CKS Prometheus integration for MaaS observability\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tDeploys Perses dashboards for MaaS metrics and integrates MaaS metrics with the xKS (CKS) Prometheus instance, making MaaS observability visible to platform administrators. Owned by the xKS Platform team per the strategy's impacted-teams table (\"observability integration with CKS Prometheus/Loki\"). Consumes the metrics instrumented in maas-api and is measured against a deployed MaaS instance on CKS.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Perses dashboards displaying MaaS observability data:\n40\t  - Token usage per subscription.\n41\t  - Rate limiting enforcement events.\n42\t  - API key lifecycle metrics (creation, validation, revocation).\n43\t- Integration with the CKS Prometheus instance: scrape configuration for the MaaS metrics endpoints.\n44\t- Confirmation that CKS Prometheus scrape targets are accessible for MaaS (a strategy assumption flagged as needing validation).\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with Perses dashboards installed, when an admin navigates to the MaaS observability dashboard, then the dashboard displays token usage per subscription, rate limiting enforcement events, and API key lifecycle metrics over the last 24 hours, measured by dashboard rendering with live data.\n49\t- The CKS Prometheus instance successfully scrapes the MaaS metrics endpoints (scrape targets healthy), or an access issue is documented and escalated to the xKS Platform / CoreWeave owners.\n50\t- Dashboards render correctly against the CKS Prometheus data source.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- HLR-8 (P0): Observability metrics functional — dashboard and CKS Prometheus integration half (the metric instrumentation itself is covered by the maas-api instrumentation epic).\n55\t\n56\t## Notes\n57\t\n58\t- Depends on CKS infrastructure assumed available per the strategy (CoreWeave standard infrastructure); accessibility is validated as part of this epic's acceptance criteria and the CKS infrastructure validation pass.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a17c4912b5196bb","agent_id":"a95517014c36948fe","session_id":"03f22d79-03f4-4cd2-8583-e4fd3448986e","uuid":"06544d77-a436-4662-aad5-a8e0873c8c5a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:09:56.207Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a04e998b15d8e4e4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
