{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-850da9f800415381","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E004\n3\ttitle: Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping for subscription tiers\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: -1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping for subscription tiers\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tMakes the mapping from OIDC token group claims to MaaS subscription tiers configurable. On RHOAI, the MaaSSubscription controller maps rate-limiting tiers to user groups via CEL predicates on the authenticated identity's groups, which come from Kubernetes RBAC. On xKS, user groups must be sourced from the OIDC token's group claim — and claim formats vary across identity providers (Entra ID uses `groups`, Cognito uses `cognito:groups`, Google Identity Platform may use custom claims). This epic makes the claim path configurable per deployment so tier/subscription management works with any standards-compliant provider. This is Tier 1 work — independent of the RHCL/Kuadrant support outcome.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Add a configurable group claim path (e.g., a `groupClaimPath` field on the Tenant CRD, defaulting to `auth.identity.groups`) passed through to the MaaSSubscription controller's CEL predicate generation, allowing per-deployment configuration without code changes.\n38\t- Tier/subscription management functional with identities sourced from OIDC group claims (subscription/tier CRUD plus tier-based rate-limit mapping).\n39\t- Fallback if the Tenant CRD cannot be extended in the MaaS 3.4-based build (the strategy flags this as needing validation): document the required claim format and push identity-provider configuration to customers, recording the limitation.\n40\t\n41\t## Acceptance Criteria\n42\t\n43\t- Given an OIDC deployment with a non-standard group claim format and the claim path configured to match that format, when a user with group membership authenticates, then the user is mapped to the appropriate subscription tier, measured by successful tier-based rate limiting enforcement.\n44\t- Subscription and tier CRUD operations work with identities sourced from OIDC group claims.\n45\t- The claim path is configurable per deployment without code changes; if the Tenant CRD is frozen in the 3.4-based build, the required claim format is documented and the limitation recorded in the known-limitations document.\n46\t- Tests cover at least two different provider claim formats (e.g., Entra ID `groups` and Cognito `cognito:groups`).\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- HLR-6 (P0): Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping (supports Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims).\n51\t- HLR-9 (P1): Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims — same controller surface and data as HLR-6 (the P1 HLR is the functional expression of the P0 capability), so both are covered by this single epic at the higher priority rather than split into two epics building the same surface.\n52\t\n53\t## Notes\n54\t\n55\t- The strategy's assumption \"OIDC group claim path can be made configurable without MaaS 3.4 GA code changes — needs validation\" is resolved during implementation: either the CRD extension lands, or the documented-claim-format fallback applies. Both outcomes are within this epic's scope, so no separate investigation is warranted.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a17c4912b5196bb","agent_id":"a95517014c36948fe","session_id":"03f22d79-03f4-4cd2-8583-e4fd3448986e","uuid":"21c47959-433b-4535-814f-22a31158c2c2","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:10:04.648Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-850da9f800415381","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
