{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83a755ebe409005a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-C-E012\n3\ttitle: Direct Envoy ext_authz integration for MaaS auth and rate limiting\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Inference Gateway\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: C\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the contingency also fails, escalate to product leadership\n16\t    and reassess the MaaS xKS Dev Preview scope per the strategy's risk mitigation\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 0\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 0\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 0\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Direct Envoy ext_authz integration for MaaS auth and rate limiting (Branch C)\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tBranch C of the RHCL/Kuadrant deployment mechanism (contingency): neither the official RHCL Helm charts nor standalone Kuadrant deployment is viable, so MaaS authentication and rate-limiting enforcement are integrated directly with Envoy ext_authz at the gateway, bypassing Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador). This reworks the MaaS-side enforcement integration while preserving the external OIDC validation and API key flows. This branch epic applies only if the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation selects outcome C.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Design and implement Envoy-native authentication enforcement via ext_authz covering the OIDC JWT validation path and the API key validation path (the maas-api callback validation flow).\n42\t- Define the rate-limiting enforcement approach without Limitador's TokenRateLimitPolicy, preserving per-subscription token rate limits with HTTP 429 on exceeded quota (or a documented equivalent).\n43\t- Preserve the strategy's identity model: customer-provided OIDC provider, API keys OIDC-independent.\n44\t- Keep changes additive/configuration-driven so RHOAI MaaS GA behavior is unchanged.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- A design for Envoy-native enforcement exists covering OIDC JWT validation and API key validation at the gateway, reviewed and recorded.\n49\t- Enforcement is integrated with the gateway on a CKS cluster with equivalent behavior to the Kuadrant path: valid OIDC tokens and API keys accepted; invalid credentials rejected; exceeded token quotas return HTTP 429 (or the documented equivalent with rationale).\n50\t- RHOAI MaaS GA behavior is unchanged (additive/configuration-driven change only).\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- HLR-7 (P0): RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (this branch realizes the contingency mechanism).\n55\t- HLR-3 (P0): Token rate limiting functional on xKS (Envoy-native enforcement path).\n56\t- HLR-4 (P0) / HLR-5 (P0): external OIDC and API key authentication remain functional under the reworked enforcement (the primary OIDC integration epic is rewritten accordingly on this branch).\n57\t\n58\t## Notes\n59\t\n60\t- This is a conditional branch epic (branch C), gated by the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation; it is attached to that investigation as a plan document and is not a standalone Jira issue.\n61\t- Gate failure impact: if the contingency also fails, the work is rewritten — escalate to product leadership and reassess the MaaS xKS Dev Preview scope, per the strategy's risk mitigation (\"lack of official RHCL support undermines the long-term viability of MaaS on xKS\").\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a17c4912b5196bb","agent_id":"a95517014c36948fe","session_id":"03f22d79-03f4-4cd2-8583-e4fd3448986e","uuid":"1bdbc6b4-8bd4-40e6-ad5a-399297c9449a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:10:08.332Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-83a755ebe409005a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
