{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ef4bf2bffdf6ffc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-A-E012\n3\ttitle: Deploy Kuadrant on xKS via official RHCL Helm charts\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Inference Gateway\n6\tteam: RHCL / OpenShift\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If RHCL does not commit official xKS support, deploy standalone\n16\t    Authorino + Limitador via upstream Helm charts instead (fallback path)\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: -1\n25\t  repo_access: 0\n26\t  architecture_claims: 0\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Low\n30\tai_implementability_score: -2\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Deploy Kuadrant on xKS via official RHCL Helm charts (Branch A)\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tBranch A of the RHCL/Kuadrant deployment mechanism: RHCL officially supports xKS and provides Helm charts. Deploys Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) on CKS — the priority platform — via the official RHCL Helm charts, with Authorino configured for external OIDC validation (replacing KubernetesTokenReview) and structured logging for authentication decisions and rate-limit enforcement. The mechanism is reusable for the AKS deployment. This branch epic applies only if the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation selects outcome A (official RHCL Helm charts committed and viable).\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Install the official RHCL/Kuadrant Helm charts on a CKS cluster with the Istio GatewayClass.\n42\t- Configure Authorino for external OIDC identity validation (issuer URL, JWKS endpoint, audience) and provide OIDC configuration guidance for the MaaS AuthPolicy integration.\n43\t- Structured logging for authentication decisions (Authorino) and rate limit enforcement (Limitador), formatted for CKS Grafana Loki aggregation.\n44\t- Validate that TokenRateLimitPolicy enforcement works on the CKS deployment (rate limiting is K8s-platform-agnostic per the strategy).\n45\t- Confirm the mechanism carries over to AKS.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) is installed via the official RHCL Helm charts on a CKS cluster, with all pods healthy.\n50\t- Authorino validates external OIDC JWTs against a configured issuer (valid tokens accepted, invalid/expired tokens rejected).\n51\t- Structured authentication-decision and rate-limit-enforcement log entries are produced and retrievable from CKS Grafana Loki.\n52\t- A MaaSSubscription with token rate limits configured returns HTTP 429 when the quota is exceeded (TokenRateLimitPolicy enforcement functional on CKS).\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- HLR-7 (P0): RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (this branch realizes the mechanism).\n57\t- HLR-3 (P0): Token rate limiting functional on xKS (Limitador enforcement path).\n58\t- HLR-10 (P1): Observability logging functional (Authorino/Limitador structured logging half).\n59\t\n60\t## Notes\n61\t\n62\t- This is a conditional branch epic (branch A), gated by the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation; it is attached to that investigation as a plan document and is not a standalone Jira issue.\n63\t- Gate failure impact: if outcome A does not hold (RHCL does not commit official xKS support), this epic is removed and the standalone Authorino + Limitador Helm deployment (branch B) applies instead.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a17c4912b5196bb","agent_id":"a95517014c36948fe","session_id":"03f22d79-03f4-4cd2-8583-e4fd3448986e","uuid":"160eb974