en a deployed MaaS instance on xKS with tracing enabled, when an inference request is made, then a trace spans gateway ingress, authentication enforcement, rate limiting, payload processing, and the model backend, measured by inspecting the collected trace data.\n45\t- maas-api trace export (OTLP/gRPC) remains functional on the xKS deployment.\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- HLR-13 (P2): Distributed tracing functional — gateway → Authorino → Limitador → payload-processing → backend.\n50\t\n51\t## Notes\n52\t\n53\t- Priority note: the strategy's NFR section labels tracing \"(P1)\" while the HLR list marks it P2; the HLR list is authoritative for this decomposition (see the decomposition summary's health warnings).\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b289c4671c74508a","agent_id":"ab94395b3c5fb0286","session_id":"03f22d79-03f4-4cd2-8583-e4fd3448986e","uuid":"f105bdac-577f-4466-9a97-d2049045fcbd","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:13:14.844Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-afa94025007864f5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
