{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad77b5b405698ddb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-B-E012\n3\ttitle: Deploy standalone Authorino and Limitador via Helm on xKS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Inference Gateway\n6\tteam: xKS Platform\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If standalone deployment is also not viable, apply the direct\n16\t    Envoy ext_authz contingency instead\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 0\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 4\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Deploy standalone Authorino and Limitador via Helm on xKS (Branch B)\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tBranch B of the RHCL/Kuadrant deployment mechanism (fallback): RHCL official xKS support is not committed, so Kuadrant's components are deployed standalone from their upstream Helm charts. Deploys Authorino and Limitador on CKS — the priority platform — owned by the xKS Platform team, with Authorino configured for external OIDC validation and structured logging for authentication decisions and rate-limit enforcement. The mechanism is reusable for the AKS deployment. This branch epic applies only if the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation selects outcome B (no official RHCL support, standalone deployment viable).\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Deploy standalone Authorino and Limitador via their upstream Helm charts on a CKS cluster with the Istio GatewayClass.\n42\t- Configure Authorino for external OIDC identity validation (issuer URL, JWKS endpoint, audience) compatible with the MaaS AuthPolicy integration.\n43\t- Structured logging for authentication decisions (Authorino) and rate limit enforcement (Limitador), formatted for CKS Grafana Loki aggregation.\n44\t- License validation of the standalone upstream components and their transitive dependencies (the strategy's license-validation prerequisite, which applies specifically on this path because upstream components are consumed directly).\n45\t- Confirm the mechanism carries over to AKS.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Standalone Authorino and Limitador are installed via Helm on a CKS cluster, with all pods healthy.\n50\t- Authorino validates external OIDC JWTs against a configured issuer (valid tokens accepted, invalid/expired tokens rejected).\n51\t- Structured authentication-decision and rate-limit-enforcement log entries are produced and retrievable from CKS Grafana Loki.\n52\t- A MaaSSubscription with token rate limits configured returns HTTP 429 when the quota is exceeded (TokenRateLimitPolicy enforcement functional on CKS).\n53\t- License validation of the standalone components and their transitive dependencies completes with no blocking findings (or findings are documented with remediation).\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- HLR-7 (P0): RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (this branch realizes the fallback mechanism).\n58\t- HLR-3 (P0): Token rate limiting functional on xKS (Limitador enforcement path).\n59\t- HLR-10 (P1): Observability logging functional (Authorino/Limitador structured logging half).\n60\t\n61\t## Notes\n62\t\n63\t- This is a conditional branch epic (branch B), gated by the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation; it is attached to that investigation as a plan document and is not a standalone Jira issue.\n64\t- Gate failure impact: if outcome B does not hold (standalone deployment also not viable), this epic is removed and the direct Envoy ext_authz contingency (branch C) applies instead.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b289c4671c74508a","agent_id":"ab94395b3c5fb0286","session_id":"03f22d79-03f4-4cd2-8583-e4fd3448986e","uuid":"722e8fb1-2c84-4a84-a6c3-da55db2c18a4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:13:20.255Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad77b5b405698ddb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
