CL/Kuadrant and a Gateway API implementation installed, when MaaS is deployed via Helm chart with OIDC configuration, then the maas-api and maas-controller pods are running and healthy, measured by pod readiness checks passing.\n45\t- Core functionality is validated on AKS: OIDC authentication, API key-based inference, subscription management, and token rate limiting (HTTP 429 on exceeded quota), measured by the same checks used for the CKS validation.\n46\t- AKS-specific known limitations and configuration differences are documented and added to the known-limitations document.\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- HLR-2 (P0): MaaS successfully deployed on AKS (RFE acceptance criterion \"AKS AND CKS\").\n51\t- HLR-11 (P1): Known limitations documented (AKS-specific findings).\n52\t\n53\t## Notes\n54\t\n55\t- The choice of Gateway API implementation on AKS (`envoy-gateway` vs. `azure-application-gateway`) is an implementation decision made when this epic starts; both are within scope.\n56\t- Runs after the CKS validation per the strategy's explicit CKS-first sequencing (priority platform); the charts and documented engineering delta from CKS are prerequisites.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2b0805231d30147","agent_id":"ab39e52713d563351","session_id":"03f22d79-03f4-4cd2-8583-e4fd3448986e","uuid":"825c3195-e624-42e2-901c-5b02d2b4d884","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:27:08.261Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f02125fcc8953b3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Final review RHAISTRAT-8003"}
