{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7e19c1f6731a7ba","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E009\n3\ttitle: Structured logging for MaaS request-path events with CKS Loki integration\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E007\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: -1\n17\t  external_dependency: -1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 0\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 3\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Structured logging for MaaS request-path events with CKS Loki integration\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tDelivers the P1 observability-logging tier: structured JSON logging across the MaaS request path — authentication decisions, rate limit enforcement, and subscription selection — integrated with CKS Grafana Loki for aggregation. This epic covers the MaaS-side events (maas-api) and the log-aggregation integration. Authorino and Limitador structured-logging configuration is carried by the selected Kuadrant deployment mechanism (official RHCL charts or standalone Kuadrant) and validated together with this epic's Loki queries; if neither Kuadrant path is viable and the direct Envoy ext_authz contingency is selected, the gateway-side enforcement logging is MaaS-owned and covered by that contingency branch instead.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Structured JSON logs in maas-api for:\n39\t  - Authentication outcomes at the API layer (success/failure, method, reason).\n40\t  - Subscription selection decisions.\n41\t  - Rate limit enforcement events (429 responses with exceeded quota).\n42\t- Log schema per the strategy: timestamp, user identity, authentication method (OIDC/API key), decision (allow/deny), and reason when denied.\n43\t- Integration with CKS Grafana Loki: log shipping/aggregation retrievable with label filters.\n44\t- Coordination with the Kuadrant deployment owners so Authorino authentication-decision logs and Limitador enforcement logs use a compatible structured format.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with structured logging enabled, when an authentication event occurs (success or failure), then the log entry includes timestamp, user identity, authentication method (OIDC/API key), decision (allow/deny), and reason (if denied), measured by querying CKS Grafana Loki with label filters.\n49\t- Rate limit enforcement events (429 with exceeded quota) and subscription selection decisions appear as structured entries retrievable from CKS Grafana Loki.\n50\t- Logging does not block the request path (asynchronous or bounded-latency emission).\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- HLR-10 (P1): Observability logging functional — authentication events, rate limit enforcement, subscription selection (MaaS-side instrumentation and Loki integration; Kuadrant-side logging configuration is part of the selected deployment mechanism, or of the Envoy ext_authz contingency branch when no Kuadrant path is selected).\n55\t\n56\t## Notes\n57\t\n58\t- CKS Grafana Loki is a strategy assumption flagged as needing validation (CoreWeave standard infrastructure); accessibility is first confirmed by the CKS infrastructure validation pass in the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation and re-confirmed by this epic's Loki-query acceptance criteria, with access issues escalated to the xKS Platform / CoreWeave owners.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2b0805231d30147","agent_id":"ab39e52713d563351","session_id":"03f22d79-03f4-4cd2-8583-e4fd3448986e","uuid":"b9c