{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88261ec89da58928","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-A-E012\n3\ttitle: Deploy Kuadrant on xKS via official RHCL Helm charts\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Inference Gateway\n6\tteam: RHCL / OpenShift\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If RHCL does not commit official xKS support, deploy standalone\n17\t    Authorino + Limitador via upstream Helm charts instead (fallback path)\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 0\n27\t  architecture_claims: 0\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Low\n31\tai_implementability_score: -2\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Deploy Kuadrant on xKS via official RHCL Helm charts (Branch A)\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tBranch A of the RHCL/Kuadrant deployment mechanism: RHCL officially supports xKS and provides Helm charts. Deploys Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) on CKS — the priority platform — via the official RHCL Helm charts, with Authorino configured for external OIDC validation (replacing KubernetesTokenReview) and structured logging for authentication decisions and rate-limit enforcement. The mechanism is reusable for the AKS deployment. This branch epic applies only if the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation selects outcome A (official RHCL Helm charts committed and viable).\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Install the official RHCL/Kuadrant Helm charts on a CKS cluster with the Istio GatewayClass.\n43\t- Configure Authorino for external OIDC identity validation (issuer URL, JWKS endpoint, audience) and provide OIDC configuration guidance for the MaaS AuthPolicy integration.\n44\t- Structured logging for authentication decisions (Authorino) and rate limit enforcement (Limitador), formatted for CKS Grafana Loki aggregation.\n45\t- Validate that TokenRateLimitPolicy enforcement works on the CKS deployment via a directly applied policy (rate limiting is K8s-platform-agnostic per the strategy); end-to-end enforcement with MaaSSubscription-configured limits is exercised during the MaaS CKS deployment validation, not re-validated here.\n46\t- Confirm the mechanism carries over to AKS.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) is installed via the official RHCL Helm charts on a CKS cluster, with all pods healthy.\n51\t- Authorino validates external OIDC JWTs against a configured issuer (valid tokens accepted, invalid/expired tokens rejected).\n52\t- Structured authentication-decision and rate-limit-enforcement log entries are produced and retrievable from CKS Grafana Loki.\n53\t- A TokenRateLimitPolicy applied directly to the deployed gateway returns HTTP 429 when the quota is exceeded, validating Limitador enforcement on the CKS deployment in isolation (end-to-end enforcement through MaaSSubscription-configured limits is validated during the MaaS CKS deployment validation).\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- HLR-7 (P0): RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (this branch realizes the mechanism).\n58\t- HLR-3 (P0): Token rate limiting functional on xKS (Limitador enforcement path).\n59\t- HLR-10 (P1): Observability logging functional (Authorino/Limitador structured logging half).\n60\t\n61\t## Notes\n62\t\n63\t- This is a conditional branch epic (branch A), gated by the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation; it is attached to that investigation as a plan document and is not a standalone Jira issue.\n64\t- Depends on the MaaS Helm chart packaging (branch-to-main-plan edge, permitted by the conditional decomposition rules): the Authorino OIDC configuration must stay compatible with the MaaS AuthPolicy integration (AuthPolicy CRs are generated by maas-controller, installed by the charts), and the deployed enforcement path targets the MaaS request path those charts deliver.\n65\t- Gate failure impact: if outcome A does not hold (RHCL does not commit official xKS support), this epic is removed and the standalone Authorino + Limitador Helm deployment (branch B) applies instead.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2b0805231d30147","agent_id":"ab39e52713d563351","session_id":"03f22d79-03f4-4cd2-8583-e4fd3448986e","uuid":"6b3248ad-3c17-43e7-937a-ae5455948864","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:27:13.664Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-88261ec89da58928","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Final review RHAISTRAT-8003"}
