{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac156a7e9eeb82f4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-B-E012\n3\ttitle: Deploy standalone Authorino and Limitador via Helm on xKS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Inference Gateway\n6\tteam: xKS Platform\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If standalone deployment is also not viable, apply the direct\n17\t    Envoy ext_authz contingency instead\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 0\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Deploy standalone Authorino and Limitador via Helm on xKS (Branch B)\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tBranch B of the RHCL/Kuadrant deployment mechanism (fallback): RHCL official xKS support is not committed, so Kuadrant's components are deployed standalone from their upstream Helm charts. Deploys Authorino and Limitador on CKS — the priority platform — owned by the xKS Platform team, with Authorino configured for external OIDC validation and structured logging for authentication decisions and rate-limit enforcement. The mechanism is reusable for the AKS deployment. This branch epic applies only if the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation selects outcome B (no official RHCL support, standalone deployment viable).\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Deploy standalone Authorino and Limitador via their upstream Helm charts on a CKS cluster with the Istio GatewayClass.\n43\t- Configure Authorino for external OIDC identity validation (issuer URL, JWKS endpoint, audience) compatible with the MaaS AuthPolicy integration.\n44\t- Structured logging for authentication decisions (Authorino) and rate limit enforcement (Limitador), formatted for CKS Grafana Loki aggregation.\n45\t- License validation of the standalone upstream components and their transitive dependencies (the strategy's license-validation prerequisite, which applies specifically on this path because upstream components are consumed directly).\n46\t- Validate that TokenRateLimitPolicy enforcement works on the CKS deployment via a directly applied policy; end-to-end enforcement with MaaSSubscription-configured limits is exercised during the MaaS CKS deployment validation, not re-validated here.\n47\t- Confirm the mechanism carries over to AKS.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Standalone Authorino and Limitador are installed via Helm on a CKS cluster, with all pods healthy.\n52\t- Authorino validates external OIDC JWTs against a configured issuer (valid tokens accepted, invalid/expired tokens rejected).\n53\t- Structured authentication-decision and rate-limit-enforcement log entries are produced and retrievable from CKS Grafana Loki.\n54\t- A TokenRateLimitPolicy applied directly to the deployed gateway returns HTTP 429 when the quota is exceeded, validating Limitador enforcement on the CKS deployment in isolation (end-to-end enforcement through MaaSSubscription-configured limits is validated during the MaaS CKS deployment validation).\n55\t- License validation of the standalone components and their transitive dependencies completes with no blocking findings (or findings are documented with remediation).\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- HLR-7 (P0): RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (this branch realizes the fallback mechanism).\n60\t- HLR-3 (P0): Token rate limiting functional on xKS (Limitador enforcement path).\n61\t- HLR-10 (P1): Observability logging functional (Authorino/Limitador structured logging half).\n62\t\n63\t## Notes\n64\t\n65\t- This is a conditional branch epic (branch B), gated by the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation; it is attached to that investigation as a plan document and is not a standalone Jira issue.\n66\t- Depends on the MaaS Helm chart packaging (branch-to-main-plan edge, permitted by the conditional decomposition rules): the Authorino OIDC configuration must stay compatible with the MaaS AuthPolicy integration (AuthPolicy CRs are generated by maas-controller, installed by the charts), and the deployed enforcement path targets the MaaS request path those charts deliver.\n67\t- Gate failure impact: if outcome B does not hold (standalone deployment also not viable), this epic is removed and the direct Envoy ext_authz contingency (branch C) applies instead.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2b0805231d30147","agent_id":"ab39e52713d563351","session_id":"03f22d79-03f4-4cd2-8583-e4fd3448986e","uuid":"3227cec4-95a6-404f-808f-9e9f50fa382e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:27:14.275Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac156a7e9eeb82f4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Final review RHAISTRAT-8003"}
